- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the admin portal as an administrator and navigate to the user management section.\n    2. Select the user whose 2FA needs to be disabled.\n    3. Click on the "Disable 2FA" option.\n    4. Confirm the pop-up prompt by clicking on "Cancel".\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    * The disablement process is cancelled, and the user\'s existing 2FA setup remains intact.\n  - **Security Impact**: Low\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    * Verifying that cancelling the disablement process does not introduce any security vulnerabilities\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    * None specific to this test scenario' context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 198, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 382, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262, 29757, 685, 279, 4074, 24007, 555, 7999, 459, 3072, 369, 38212, 311, 11404, 1403, 75197, 17066, 320, 17, 3711, 8, 369, 3927, 3932, 13, 3277, 459, 4074, 50243, 420, 3072, 11, 10137, 369, 20109, 1603, 39547, 13, 30538, 20109, 11, 4148, 279, 6484, 220, 17, 3711, 6642, 369, 279, 1217, 11, 10923, 1124, 311, 312, 21678, 220, 17, 3711, 422, 4460, 627, 11859, 709, 198, 11787, 499, 2771, 499, 1390, 311, 11404, 1403, 75197, 17066, 320, 17, 3711, 8, 369, 420, 1217, 5380, 9290, 25, 4185, 19295, 220, 17, 3711, 690, 4148, 872, 1510, 17066, 6642, 11, 323, 814, 690, 1205, 311, 743, 433, 709, 1578, 13, 1115, 1957, 4250, 387, 79841, 13, 578, 1217, 2011, 312, 21678, 220, 17, 3711, 369, 9966, 2680, 627, 13245, 512, 17143, 612, 29127, 320, 16352, 5703, 482, 41870, 449, 409, 23863, 340, 9453, 320, 50063, 5703, 482, 4185, 1869, 279, 22727, 696, 262, 3146, 5207, 15392, 334, 512, 262, 55375, 61173, 198, 262, 17010, 14026, 25, 510, 3413, 4076, 933, 262, 482, 3146, 2323, 59763, 96618, 510, 55131, 7817, 933, 415, 482, 3146, 2323, 11799, 3110, 96618, 25610, 42095, 6277, 60, 720, 415, 482, 3146, 21197, 96618, 393, 15, 320, 43108, 5738, 4