DEBUG:root:Ollama raw response: model='llama3' created_at='2025-03-11T06:43:42.4207811Z' done=True done_reason='stop' total_duration=403813536300 load_duration=3641450400 prompt_eval_count=316 prompt_eval_duration=88836000000 eval_count=634 eval_duration=311323000000 response='Here are the comprehensive test scenarios for the given requirement:\n\n### Module: Admin Portal Enhancements\n#### Test Scenario: Disable Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) for Individual Users\n- **Test Case ID**: TC-01 \n- **Priority**: P0 (Critical)\n- **Preconditions**:\n\t+ The admin portal is accessible and logged in with an administrator account.\n\t+ A user exists in the system with 2FA setup enabled.\n- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the admin portal as an administrator.\n    2. Navigate to the user management section and select a user who has 2FA setup enabled.\n    3. Click on the "Disable 2FA" option for that user.\n\t4. A popup appears with a confirmation message: "Are you sure you want to disable two-factor authentication (2FA) for this user?"\n    5. Confirm the deactivation by clicking "Confirm & Disable".\n- **Expected Results**:\n\t+ The existing 2FA setup is removed for the selected user.\n\t+ The user must reconfigure their 2FA setup to regain secure access.\n\t+ No errors or exceptions are reported during the process.\n- **Security Impact**: High\n- **Edge Cases Covered**:\n\t+ Test with different types of 2FA setups (e.g., Google Authenticator, SMS-based).\n\t+ Verify that disabling 2FA for a user does not affect their login credentials or other system settings.\n- **Compliance Checks**:\n\t+ Ensure that the deactivation process meets relevant security and compliance standards (e.g., GDPR, HIPAA).\n\n### Module: Admin Portal Enhancements\n#### Test Scenario: Cancel Disable 2FA Confirmation Popup\n- **Test Case ID**: TC-02 \n- **Priority**: P1 (High)\n- **Preconditions**:\n\t+ The admin portal is accessible and logged in with an administrator account.\n\t+ A user exists in the system with 2FA setup enabled.\n- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the admin portal as an administrator.\n    2. Navigate to the user management section and select a user who has 2FA setup enabled.\n    3. Click on the "Disable 2FA" option for that user.\n\t4. A popup appears with a confirmation message: "Are you sure you want to disable two-factor authentication (2FA) for this user?"\n\t5. Cancel the deactivation by clicking "Cancel".\n- **Expected Results**:\n\t+ The disable 2FA process is cancelled, and the existing 2FA setup remains enabled.\n\t+ No errors or exceptions are reported during the cancellation process.\n- **Security Impact**: Medium\n- **Edge Cases Covered**:\n\t+ Verify that cancelling the deactivation process does not affect other system settings.\n- **Compliance Checks**:\n\t+ Ensure that the cancellation process meets relevant security and compliance standards (e.g., GDPR, HIPAA).\n\nNote: These test scenarios focus on verifying the correct functioning of the disable 2FA feature and its associated popup.' context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 198, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 382, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262, 29757, 685, 279, 4074, 24007, 555, 7999, 459, 3072, 369, 38212, 311, 11404, 1403, 75197, 17066, 320, 17, 3711, 8, 369, 3927, 3932, 13, 3277, 459, 4074, 50243, 420, 3072, 11, 10137, 369, 20109, 1603, 39547, 13, 30538, 20109, 11, 4148, 279, 6484, 220, 17, 3711, 6642, 369, 279, 1217, 11, 10923, 1124, 311, 312, 21678, 220, 17, 3711, 422, 4460, 627, 11859, 709, 198, 11787, 499, 2771, 499, 1390, 311, 11404, 1403, 75197, 17066, 320, 17, 3711, 8, 369, 420, 1217, 5380, 9290, 25, 4185, 19295, 220, 17, 3711, 690, 4148, 872, 1510, 17066, 6642, 11, 323, 814, 690, 1205, 311, 743, 433, 709, 1578, 13, 1115, 1957, 4250, 387, 79841, 13, 578, 1217, 2011, 312, 21678, 220, 17, 3711, 369, 9966, 2680, 627, 13245, 512, 17143,