DEBUG:root:Ollama raw response: model='llama3' created_at='2025-03-11T07:08:09.127268Z' done=True done_reason='stop' total_duration=202400964700 load_duration=52560300 prompt_eval_count=315 prompt_eval_duration=17627000000 eval_count=695 eval_duration=184720000000 response='Here are the comprehensive test scenarios for the requirement:\n\n### Module: Admin Portal - Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) Disabling\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Verify that administrators can successfully disable 2FA for individual users, prompting for confirmation before proceeding.\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-001\n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    * The admin portal is accessible with valid credentials.\n    * A user has existing 2FA setup.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the admin portal as an administrator.\n    2. Navigate to the user\'s profile and click on the "Disable 2FA" option.\n    3. Confirm the prompt by clicking "Confirm & Disable".\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    * The existing 2FA setup is removed for the selected user.\n    * The user must reconfigure 2FA to regain access.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    * Disabling 2FA for a user with multiple authenticators (e.g., Google Authenticator, SMS-based).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    * Verify that the system logs the action and provides an audit trail.\n\n### Module: Admin Portal - Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) Disabling\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Verify that administrators cannot disable 2FA for individual users without confirmation.\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-002\n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    * The admin portal is accessible with valid credentials.\n    * A user has existing 2FA setup.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the admin portal as an administrator.\n    2. Navigate to the user\'s profile and click on the "Disable 2FA" option.\n    3. Click "Cancel" without confirming the prompt.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    * The existing 2FA setup remains intact for the selected user.\n  - **Security Impact**: Low\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    * Canceling the confirmation prompt before disabling 2FA.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    * Verify that the system logs the attempted action and provides an audit trail.\n\n### Module: Admin Portal - Two-Factor Authentication (2FA) Disabling\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Verify that administrators cannot disable 2FA for users without existing 2FA setup.\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-003\n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    * The admin portal is accessible with valid credentials.\n    * A user does not have existing 2FA setup.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the admin portal as an administrator.\n    2. Navigate to the user\'s profile and click on the "Disable 2FA" option.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    * The system displays an error message indicating that the user does not have existing 2FA setup.\n  - **Security Impact**: Low\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    * Disabling 2FA for a user without existing 2FA setup.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    * Verify that the system logs the attempted action and provides an audit trail.' context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 198, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 382, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262, 29757, 685, 279, 4074, 24007, 555, 7999, 459, 3072, 369, 38212, 311, 11404, 1403, 75197, 17066, 320, 17, 3711, 8, 369, 3927, 3932, 13, 3277, 459, 4074, 50243, 420, 3072, 11, 10137, 369, 20109, 1603, 39547, 13, 30538, 20109, 11, 4148, 279, 6484, 220, 17, 3711, 6642, 369, 279, 1217, 11, 10923, 1124, 311, 312, 21678, 220, 17, 3711, 422, 4460, 13, 10466, 709, 8886, 499, 2771, 499, 1390, 311, 11404, 1403, 75197, 17066, 320, 17, 3711, 8, 369, 420, 1217, 30, 7181, 25, 4185, 19295, 220, 17, 3711, 690, 4148, 872, 1510, 17066, 6642, 11, 323, 814, 690, 1205, 311, 743, 433, 709, 1578, 13, 1115, 19