eas.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Invalid username and password combination.\n    - Username only (password omitted).\n    - Password only (username omitted).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system logs the failed sign-in attempt.\n    - Check that the system enforces rate limiting to prevent brute-force attacks.\n\n### Module: Sign In\n- **Test Scenario**: Forgotten Password Recovery\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-SIGNIN-003 \n  - **Priority**: P2 (Medium)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user has a valid account with the system.\n    - The user\'s password is forgotten or needs to be reset.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Navigate to the sign-in page.\n    2. Click the "Forgot Password" link.\n    3. Enter the username associated with the forgotten password.\n    4. Follow the system\'s instructions for resetting the password.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system sends a password reset email or displays a temporary password.\n    - The user can reset their password and gain access to their account.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Valid username and correct email address.\n    - Invalid username and correct email address.\n    - Correct username and invalid email address.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system logs the password reset request.\n    - Check that the system enforces password policies (e.g., length, complexity) for new passwords.\n\nThese test scenarios cover various sign-in scenarios, including successful and unsuccessful attempts, as well as forgotten password recovery. They also highlight security implications, edge cases, and compliance checks to ensure comprehensive testing of the sign-in feature.' context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 198, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 382, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262