DEBUG:root:Ollama raw response: model='llama3' created_at='2025-03-11T12:15:04.3071917Z' done=True done_reason='stop' total_duration=385241228400 load_duration=9049344400 prompt_eval_count=173 prompt_eval_duration=14747000000 eval_count=1356 eval_duration=361434000000 response='Here are the comprehensive test scenarios for the login page:\n\n```markdown\n### Module: Login Page\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Valid User Credentials\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-01 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is not logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Enter valid username and password credentials.\n    2. Click the login button.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The user is successfully logged in.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the login credentials are stored securely.\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Invalid User Credentials\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-02 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is not logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Enter invalid username and password credentials.\n    2. Click the login button.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system displays an error message indicating incorrect login credentials.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system logs failed login attempts.\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Forgot Password\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-03 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is not logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Click the "Forgot password" link.\n    2. Enter valid username and click submit.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system displays a password reset page with instructions.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system sends a password reset email to the user\'s registered email address.\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Logout\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-04 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Click the logout button.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The user is successfully logged out.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system clears sensitive information after logout.\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Session Time-Out\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-05 \n  - **Priority**: P2 (Medium)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Set the session timeout to a short duration (e.g., 5 minutes).\n    2. Perform other actions on the system while the session is still active.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system logs the user out after the session times out.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system complies with security standards for session management.\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) Attack\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-06 \n  - **Priority**: P2 (Medium)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Create a simple HTML page with a form that submits a malicious request to the login page.\n    2. Open two browser windows: one for the test page and another for the system\'s login page.\n    3. Fill out the form on the test page and submit it.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system does not log the user out or perform any unauthorized actions.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system complies with security standards for CSRF protection.\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Login Page XSS Vulnerability\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-07 \n  - **Priority**: P2 (Medium)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is not logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Create a simple HTML page with malicious script that attempts to inject JavaScript into the login page.\n    2. Open two browser windows: one for the test page and another for the system\'s login page.\n    3. Fill out the form on the test page and submit it.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system does not execute the malicious script or perform any unauthorized actions.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system complies with security standards for XSS protection.\n\n- **Test Scenario**: Login Page SQL Injection Vulnerability\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-08 \n  - **Priority**: P2 (Medium)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    - The user is not logged in.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Create a simple HTML page with malicious script that attempts to inject SQL code into the login page.\n    2. Open two browser windows: one for the test page and another for the system\'s login page.\n    3. Fill out the form on the test page and submit it.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    - The system does not execute the malicious script or perform any unauthorized actions.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Test with different types of input data (e.g., numbers, special characters).\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    - Verify that the system complies with security standards for SQL injection protection.' context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 5839