DEBUG:root:Ollama raw response: model='llama3' created_at='2025-03-11T12:19:08.0879185Z' done=True done_reason='stop' total_duration=324477698500 load_duration=76521400 prompt_eval_count=178 prompt_eval_duration=18667000000 eval_count=991 eval_duration=305731000000 response='Here are the comprehensive test scenarios for the requirement "User should be able to reset their password via email":\n\n### Module: Password Reset via Email\n- **Test Scenario**: Verify that users can successfully reset their passwords via email.\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-PW01 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    * The user has a valid account with the system.\n    * The user\'s email address is correctly associated with their account.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the system using a valid username and password.\n    2. Click on the "Forgot Password" link.\n    3. Enter the correct email address associated with the user\'s account.\n    4. Submit the request to reset the password.\n    5. Verify that an email is sent to the user\'s registered email address with a password reset link.\n    6. Open the email and click on the password reset link.\n    7. Enter a new password and confirm it.\n    8. Click "Reset Password" to update the password.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    * The user\'s password is successfully updated in the system.\n    * The user can log in with their new password.\n  - **Security Impact**: High\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    * Users with invalid or expired email addresses.\n    * Users who have not verified their email address.\n    * Users who have multiple accounts with different email addresses.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    * Verify that the password reset link is generated and sent securely (e.g., using HTTPS).\n    * Confirm that the system logs all password reset attempts, including successes and failures.\n\n### Module: Password Reset via Email - Invalid Email\n- **Test Scenario**: Verify that users cannot reset their passwords via email with an invalid or unverified email address.\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-PW02 \n  - **Priority**: P1 (High)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    * The user has a valid account with the system.\n    * The user\'s email address is not correctly associated with their account.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to the system using a valid username and password.\n    2. Click on the "Forgot Password" link.\n    3. Enter an invalid or unverified email address (e.g., one that does not exist or is not linked to their account).\n    4. Submit the request to reset the password.\n    5. Verify that no email is sent or that the system denies the request.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    * The system does not send an email for password reset and/or denies the request.\n    * The user\'s password remains unchanged.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    * Users who have multiple accounts with different email addresses.\n    * Users who have previously used a different email address for their account.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    * Verify that the system logs all failed password reset attempts, including invalid or unverified email addresses.\n\n### Module: Password Reset via Email - Multiple Accounts\n- **Test Scenario**: Verify that users with multiple accounts can only reset passwords for one account at a time.\n  - **Test Case ID**: TC-PW03 \n  - **Priority**: P2 (Medium)\n  - **Preconditions**:\n    * The user has two or more valid accounts with the system.\n    * Each account has its own unique email address.\n  - **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in to one of the accounts using a valid username and password.\n    2. Click on the "Forgot Password" link.\n    3. Enter the correct email address associated with the current account.\n    4. Submit the request to reset the password.\n    5. Verify that an email is sent to the registered email address for the current account.\n    6. Repeat steps 1-5 for another account, using a different email address.\n    7. Verify that no email is sent or that the system denies the request for the second account.\n  - **Expected Results**:\n    * The user can only reset their password for one account at a time.\n    * The system does not allow multiple password resets to occur simultaneously.\n  - **Security Impact**: Medium\n  - **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    * Users who have previously used different email addresses for their accounts.\n    * Users who have merged or deleted accounts in the past.\n  - **Compliance Checks**:\n    * Verify that the system logs all multiple password reset attempts, including those that are denied.\n\nPlease note that these test scenarios are just a starting point and may need to be modified based on specific requirements and constraints.' context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 198, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 382, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262, 2724, 1288, 387, 3025, 311, 7738, 872, 3636, 4669, 2613, 382, 262, 3146, 5207, 15392, 334, 512, 262, 55375, 61173, 198, 262, 17010, 14026, 25, 510, 3413, 4076, 933, 262, 482, 3146, 2323, 59763, 96618, 510, 55131, 7817, 933, 415, 482, 3146, 2323, 11799, 3110, 96618, 25610, 42095, 6277, 60, 720, 415, 482, 3146, 21197, 96618, 393, 15, 320, 43108, 5738, 47, 16, 320, 12243, 5738, 47, 17, 320, 42094, 340, 415, 482, 3146, 4808, 16902, 96618, 720, 415, 482, 3146, 2323, 40961, 334, 512, 286, 220, 16, 13, 720, 286, 220, 17, 13, 720, 415, 482, 3146, 19430, 18591, 334, 512, 415, 482, 3146, 15712, 29680, 96618, 510, 12243, 10482, 23961, 7586, 363, 933, 415, 482, 3146, 11918, 47124, 73295, 334, 512, 415, 482, 3146, 1110, 32712, 25884, 334, 512, 262, 42333, 257, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271, 8586, 527, 279, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 16686, 330, 1502, 1288, 387, 3025, 311, 7738, 872, 3636, 4669, 2613, 52518, 14711, 14026, 25, 12642, 17362, 4669, 8463, 198, 12, 3146, 2323, 59763, 96618