DEBUG:root:Ollama raw response: model='llama3' created_at='2025-03-12T04:28:11.034392Z' done=True done_reason='stop' total_duration=259834373800 load_duration=9513139900 prompt_eval_count=271 prompt_eval_duration=21579000000 eval_count=915 eval_duration=228731000000 response="Here are the comprehensive test scenarios for the given requirement:\n\n### Module: Disposable Email Address Restriction Policy\n#### Test Scenario 1: Valid Email Address Registration\n- **Test Case ID**: TC-DISP001 \n- **Priority**: P0 (Critical)\n- **Preconditions**: None\n- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Attempt to register with a valid email address (e.g., example@gmail.com).\n    2. Verify that the registration is successful and the account is created.\n- **Expected Results**: The account creation process completes without errors, and the user can access their newly created account.\n- **Security Impact**: Low\n- **Edge Cases Covered**: None\n- **Compliance Checks**:\n#### Test Scenario 2: Disposable Email Address Registration (Blocked Domain)\n- **Test Case ID**: TC-DISP002 \n- **Priority**: P0 (Critical)\n- **Preconditions**: The system has a regularly updated blacklist of known disposable email domains.\n- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Attempt to register with a disposable email address (e.g., tempmail123@trashmail.com).\n    2. Verify that the registration is rejected and an error message is displayed prompting the user to use a valid email address.\n- **Expected Results**: The account creation process fails, and an error message is displayed indicating that the email address is invalid.\n- **Security Impact**: High\n- **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Edge case 1: Attempting to register with multiple disposable email addresses in rapid succession.\n    - Edge case 2: Using a disposable email address from a recently updated blacklist.\n- **Compliance Checks**:\n\n### Module: Disposable Email Address Restriction Policy (Continued)\n#### Test Scenario 3: Valid Email Address Authentication\n- **Test Case ID**: TC-DISP003 \n- **Priority**: P0 (Critical)\n- **Preconditions**: The system has a regularly updated blacklist of known disposable email domains.\n- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Log in with a valid email address (e.g., example@gmail.com).\n    2. Verify that the login process completes successfully and access to the account is granted.\n- **Expected Results**: The user can log in successfully, and access their account without errors.\n- **Security Impact**: Low\n- **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Edge case 1: Attempting to authenticate with a disposable email address after previously logging in with a valid email address.\n- **Compliance Checks**:\n\n### Module: Disposable Email Address Restriction Policy (Continued)\n#### Test Scenario 4: Notification for Disposable Email Address\n- **Test Case ID**: TC-DISP004 \n- **Priority**: P0 (Critical)\n- **Preconditions**: The system has a regularly updated blacklist of known disposable email domains.\n- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Attempt to register with a disposable email address (e.g., tempmail123@trashmail.com).\n    2. Verify that the registration is rejected, and an error message is displayed prompting the user to use a valid email address.\n- **Expected Results**: The system displays a notification indicating that the email address is invalid and cannot be used for account creation.\n- **Security Impact**: High\n- **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Edge case 1: Displaying multiple notifications in rapid succession when attempting to register with disposable email addresses.\n- **Compliance Checks**:\n\n### Module: Disposable Email Address Restriction Policy (Continued)\n#### Test Scenario 5: System Configuration and Monitoring\n- **Test Case ID**: TC-DISP005 \n- **Priority**: P1 (High)\n- **Preconditions**: The system is configured to block disposable email addresses.\n- **Test Steps**:\n    1. Verify that the system's configuration settings for blocking disposable email addresses are correctly set.\n    2. Monitor the system for a period of time to ensure that it is effectively blocking disposable email addresses and rejecting attempts to register or authenticate with such addresses.\n- **Expected Results**: The system correctly blocks disposable email addresses, and rejects attempts to register or authenticate with them.\n- **Security Impact**: High\n- **Edge Cases Covered**:\n    - Edge case 1: Configuring the system to block disposable email addresses in different environments (e.g., staging, production).\n- **Compliance Checks**:\n\nThese test scenarios cover the main requirements of the disposable email address restriction policy and ensure that the system effectively blocks known disposable email domains." context=[128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 198, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 382, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262, 77038, 25, 32175, 264, 20020, 4947, 311, 2565, 279, 1005, 315, 44890, 2613, 14564, 369, 2759, 12506, 323, 17066, 311, 18885, 4868, 323, 5471, 54983, 7640, 13, 578, 1887, 1288, 10765, 323, 8007, 3967, 44890, 2613, 31576, 1701, 264, 15870, 6177, 67149, 11, 54952, 4948, 24993, 34456, 477, 20958, 459, 5419, 1160, 13, 14969, 19969, 311, 4254, 449, 44890, 14633, 1288, 5371, 264, 11801, 50745, 1124, 311, 1005, 264, 2764, 2613, 2686, 13, 578, 4947, 1288, 387, 20336, 11, 12793, 304, 264, 48862, 4676, 11, 323, 27167, 311, 5788, 11, 449, 14529, 16967, 323, 9013, 311, 279, 19857, 8106, 1160, 311, 6106, 27375, 382, 262, 3146, 5207, 15392, 334, 512, 262, 55375, 61173, 198, 262, 17010, 14026, 25, 510, 3413, 4076, 933, 262, 482, 3146, 2323, 59763, 96618, 510, 55131, 7817, 933, 415, 482, 3146, 2323, 11799, 3110, 96618, 25610, 42095, 6277, 60, 720, 415, 482, 3146, 21197, 96618, 393, 15, 320, 43108, 5738, 47, 16, 320, 12243, 5738, 47, 17, 320, 42094, 340, 415, 482, 3146, 4808, 16902, 96618, 720, 415, 482, 3146, 2323, 40961, 334, 512, 286, 220, 16, 13, 720, 286