DEBUG:root:Ollama raw response: model='llama3.2:1b' created_at='2025-03-13T06:03:05.8318648Z' done=True done_reason='stop' total_duration=69027124800 load_duration=4387942800 prompt_eval_count=298 prompt_eval_duration=2418000000 eval_count=930 eval_duration=62219000000 response="Here is the comprehensive test scenario for the requirement to implement a restriction policy for disposable email addresses:\n\n### Module: Security Policy Enforcement\n\n#### Test Scenario: Disposable Email Address Policy Enforcement\n\n```markdown\n### Test Scenario: Disposable Email Address Policy Enforcement\n\n#### **Test Case ID:** TC-001\n#### **Priority:** P0 (Critical)\n\n#### **Preconditions:**\n\n* The system is configured with a regularly updated blacklist of disposable email domains.\n* A valid email address has been added to the user's account.\n\n#### **Test Steps:**\n\n1. Attempt to register a new user with a known disposable email domain using a third-party API or an internal list (e.g., `example.com`).\n2. Verify that the user receives a notification prompting them to use a valid email address.\n3. Verify that the system rejects the registration attempt for the known disposable email domain.\n\n#### **Expected Results:**\n\n* The system successfully rejects the registration attempt for the known disposable email domain (`example.com`).\n* The user does not receive any further notifications or alerts regarding the registration attempt.\n* The system correctly identifies and blocks the `example.com` domain from future registrations.\n\n#### **Security Impact:** High\n```\n\n### Module: Compliance Policy Enforcement\n\n```markdown\n### Module: Compliance Policy Enforcement\n\n#### Test Scenario: Disposable Email Address Policy Compliance\n\n```markdown\n#### **Test Case ID:** TC-002\n#### **Priority:** P1 (High)\n\n#### **Preconditions:**\n\n* The system is configured to integrate with a third-party API that provides real-time email address information.\n* An internal list of disposable email domains has been maintained.\n\n#### **Test Steps:**\n\n1. Attempt to register a new user using an external email address provider (e.g., `test@example.net`).\n2. Verify that the system recognizes the registered email address as valid and allows registration.\n3. Verify that the system correctly adds the registered email address to the user's account information.\n\n#### **Expected Results:**\n\n* The system successfully registers the new user with a valid email address using an external provider.\n* The system correctly adds the registered email address to the user's account information in the internal list of disposable domains.\n\n#### **Compliance Checks:**\n\n* The system is configured to use a regularly updated blacklist of disposable email domains.\n```\n\n### Module: Edge Case and Boundary Value Testing\n\n```markdown\n### Module: Edge Case and Boundary Value Testing\n\n#### Test Scenario: Disposable Email Address Policy Enforcement (Edge Cases)\n\n```markdown\n#### **Test Case ID:** TC-003\n#### **Priority:** P2 (Medium)\n\n#### **Preconditions:**\n\n* The system is configured with a regularly updated blacklist of disposable email domains.\n* A valid email address has been added to the user's account.\n\n#### **Test Steps:**\n\n1. Attempt to register a new user using an extremely long or unusual email address (e.g., `example.co.uk`).\n2. Verify that the system correctly rejects the registration attempt for the known disposable email domain (`example.com`).\n3. Verify that the system does not allow registration of users with extremely long or unusual email addresses.\n4. Verify that the user receives a notification prompting them to use a valid email address.\n\n#### **Expected Results:**\n\n* The system successfully rejects the registration attempt for an extremely long or unusual email address (`example.co.uk`).\n* The user does not receive any further notifications or alerts regarding the registration attempt.\n```\n\n### Module: Ongoing Monitoring and Updates\n\n```markdown\n### Module: Ongoing Monitoring and Updates\n\n#### Test Scenario: Disposable Email Address Policy Enforcement (Ongoing)\n\n```markdown\n#### **Test Case ID:** TC-004\n#### **Priority:** P0 (Critical)\n\n#### **Preconditions:**\n\n* The system is configured with a regularly updated blacklist of disposable email domains.\n* A valid email address has been added to the user's account.\n\n#### **Test Steps:**\n\n1. Attempt to register a new user using an external email address provider (e.g., `test@example.net`).\n2. Verify that the system recognizes the registered email address as invalid and blocks future registrations.\n3. Verify that the system correctly adds the registered email address to the user's account information.\n\n#### **Expected Results:**\n\n* The system successfully registers the new user with an invalid email address using an external provider.\n* The system correctly blocks future registrations of users with the same external email address provider.\n```\n\nNote that these test scenarios are just a starting point, and additional scenarios may be required to cover all edge cases and boundary values." context=[128006, 9125, 128007, 271, 38766, 1303, 33025, 2696, 25, 6790, 220, 2366, 18, 271, 128009, 128006, 882, 128007, 1432, 262, 3146, 9207, 96618, 19903, 67008, 29483, 58394, 304, 4868, 323, 8907, 7649, 2355, 262, 3146, 6396, 96618, 20400, 16195, 1296, 26350, 369, 279, 2728, 16686, 13, 19124, 262, 3146, 76902, 12051, 334, 512, 262, 16686, 4424, 794, 330, 64080, 264, 20020, 4947, 311, 2565, 279, 1005, 315, 44890, 2613, 14564, 369, 2759, 12506, 323, 17066, 311, 18885, 4868, 323, 5471, 54983, 7640, 13, 578, 1887, 1288, 10765, 323, 8007, 3967, 44890, 2613, 31576, 1701, 264, 15870, 6177, 67149, 11, 54952, 4948, 24993, 34456, 477, 20958, 459, 5419, 1160, 13, 14969, 19969, 311, 4254, 449, 44890, 14633, 1288, 5371, 264, 11801, 50745, 1124, 311, 1005, 264, 2764, 2613, 2686, 13, 578, 4947, 1288, 387, 20336, 11, 12793, 304,